WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:06.160
Element 118, Ununoctium or Uuo,

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:08.640
is the last element in the Periodic Table,

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:14.850
and it's in the group which contains the noble gases,

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:18.600
going from Helium right down to radioactive Radon,

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:22.400
so it is going to be radioactive.

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:26.840
So far, only 3 Atoms, have been observed.

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:32.400
First one Atom then another two. So it's more than Ununquadium,

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:39.760
is it more? It's more than Ununquadium, where we had,

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:43.240
only one Atom, but  it's still not very many Atoms.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:51.200
It's still arguable whether it will be a gass-like Radon,

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:56.320
or it may be a solid, just like some of the other elements,

00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:58.000
perhaps a solid that's rather volatile.

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:03.320
So that it would evaporate easily. But nobody knows.

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:06.760
How can you know 118  is the last element,

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:10.360
on the Periodic Table? -Well formally,

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:16.520
they could be heavier elements than 118, but the electrons,

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:20.320
the negatively charged particles, that surround,

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:25.800
the positively charged nucleus, are in shells,

00:01:26.840 --> 00:01:30.000
which gradually go outwards. Rather like the skins,

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:38.800
of an onion. So that element 118,

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:42.880
represents the whole of a shell, being filled.

00:01:43.630 --> 00:01:46.280
So we know that there are no more electrons,

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:54.970
that can be easily accommodated and if we make element 119,

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:58.880
which would be an alkali metal like sodium or cesium,

00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:02.000
then we would have to put a single electron,

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:04.980
a lot further away, from the nucleus.

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:07.680
And as soon as you start adding electrons,

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:09.920
that are further away, the whole system,

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:13.320
is expected to become very much less stable.

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:17.640
So if we can only make  3 Atoms of element 118,

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:20.760
something that's going to be very much less stable,

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:26.140
is not likely to be found in the short time.

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:27.920
Though one of the  exciting things about science,

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:30.800
is that the unexpected often happens.

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:35.120
So, it might be that before  we've started updating,

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:39.920
some of these videos, element 119 will be announced.

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:42.200
And nobody will be more excited than me.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:48.400
